```

`price_after_discount_and_tax()` in `shop/pricing.py` called `apply_tax()` on the discounted subtotal internally, so any caller that subsequently applied tax again (or fed that result into `cart.total()`) would charge tax twice. Fixed by removing the `apply_tax()` call from the helper so it returns only the post-discount subtotal — tax is applied exactly once by `cart.total()`. Added `tests/test_issue_2.py` with 7 tests (3 fail before fix, all pass after); full suite green (42 passed).
@m13-board
